#Information Gathering via facts

-- Gathering Facts
	- Key-value pairs of data
	- IP Addressing
	- Drive info
	- Current OS etc.

-- Create a new file(gather-facts.yml)
------------Start of file-----------
---
- name: Gather facts and display it
  hosts: LL-rocky9-01
  tasks:
  - name: Display all gathered facts
    ansible.builtin.debug:
      var: ansible_facts

  - name: Display the currently running kernel version and distro
    ansible.builtin.debug
      msg: "The kernel version is {{ ansible_facts.kernel }} and the distribution is {{ ansible_facts.distribution }}
--------------End of file------------

-- Run ansible-playbook -i inventory gather-facts.yml
-- Go through gather facts modules. 
Note* This is useful for creating reports of the machines. 	
		

# Simple Config Management

* Tasks: Create a web server to display hello world!

-- Create a new file (webserver.yml)
--------------start of file--------------
---
- name: Quick webserver install and config
  hosts: LL-rocky9-01
  gather_facts: false
  become: true
  tasks:
    - name: Install apache webserver
      ansible.builtin.package:
        name: httpd
        state: present


    - name: Start and enable apache
      ansible.builtin.service:
        name: httpd
        state: started
        enabled: true

    - name: Write a simple index.html file
      ansible.builtin.lineinfile
        path: /var/www/html/index/html
        line: "<h1>Hello World!<h1>"
        create: true
-----------End of file----------------

-- Save the file. 

run ansible-playbook -i inventory webserver.yml

run curl http://Ip of the machine  
* to validate the server is running and configured correctly. 

#Idempotence

* I can rerun a piece of automation as many times as I want and it will only
  make change when necessary.

-- Idempotence Output

ok			Everything executed fine, and no changes were made.
changed			Everything executed fine, and the automation made a change to the host. 
failed			The task failed for a host. This will cause  the playbook to show a failed status.
skipping		This task had a conditional set, and the host didn't match,
			so it skipped for this specific host. 

-- Idempotence Caveat

- Not all modules are idempotent
- Example: shell module
- Example shell command: echo hello > hello.txt

--Create a test file(idempotent.yml)
-----------------Start of file------------
---
- name: Testing idempotence
  hosts: LL-rocky09-01
  gather_facts: false
  tasks:
   - name: Use shell to echo hello to hello.txt
     ansible.builtin.shell: echo hello > /tmp/hello.txt
-------------------End of File--------------

- Save a file

run ansible-playbook -i inventory idempotent.yml
--Output: changed
run again and observe the output

# Using Variables, Conditionals and Loops

-- Variables
	- Information gathering
	- Adds flexibility
	- {{ variable_name_here }}
	- 22 levels of variable precedence
	- I placed username/passwords in inventory
	- Example: set_facts module, vars section, registering contents of task.
-- create a file(vcl.yml)
--------Start of file------------
---
- name: Vars, conditionals, and loops
  hosts: LL-rocky9-01
  gather_facts: false
  vars:
    nums:
      - 1
      - 10
      - 20
      - 25
      - 30
   tasks:
     - name: Display any numbers larger than 10
       when: item > 10		// Conditional statement
       ansible.builtin.debug:
         msg: "{{ item }}"
       loop: "{{ nums }}"
----------End of file-------------
- save the file and then run it. 

-- Condtionals
